        "mode": "DIRECT_HELP"
      },
      "output": {
        "message": "Here is a straightforward way to handle it: 1. **Pick one neutral sentence and stick to it word-for-word.** Something simple like: \"I keep my dating life private, but if there's ever news to share, you'll know.\" Repeating the exact same words each time gives them zero new hooks to keep prying.\n2. **Don't explain or justify.** Explaining why you want privacy usually sounds like an invitation to debate. State your line calmly, then let the silence sit or move on.\n3. **Have a low-drama exit ready.** If they push past the boundary, casually step away instead of arguing: \"I'm going to head to my room to wrap some things up\" or go grab a glass of water. Consistency is what makes boundaries stick when living together. Pick the phrase that feels most natural to you and treat it like your default script.",
