      "output": {
        "message": "Here is a practical structure you can adapt to your own style: 1. **Pick a neutral moment.** Bring it up when no one has just asked about dating and tensions are low, so it doesn't feel like a reaction to an argument.\n2. **State the request directly without over-explaining.** Keep the focus on what you want going forward: *\"I want to talk about something simply. I’ve decided to keep my personal and dating life private while living here. I’m asking you to stop asking about it.\"*\n3. **Decide your close ahead of time.** If they push back or demand to know why, you don't have to defend it. A simple *\"There’s nothing to debate, I just wanted to be clear with you\"* lets you state your position and walk away if needed. You can tweak the words so they sound like you, but keeping it direct and brief gives them the least room to push back.",
